{"reference":"Revelation 6","book":"Revelation","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Prophetic Echoes","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The cosmic upheaval of verses 12–17 may echo prophetic imagery associated with Joel, while its language and motifs can also be compared with Zephaniah. These are plausible cumulative allusions, not explicit quotations: the precise relationship—direct quotation, shared tradition, or broader prophetic reuse—must be weighed passage by passage.","verse_refs":["Revelation 6:12-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_006_169f248fa0b242dc68a8c92c","reader_path_revelation_006_1868de414ad3339a63d87d83"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Revelation’s Larger Pattern","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Elsewhere in Revelation, the book repeatedly reworks Israel’s Scriptures, especially Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. Its seals, trumpets, and bowls also form major sevenfold judgment sequences, with interludes and recurring motifs.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 14:1-20","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 16:1-21","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 22:1-21","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 4:1-11","Revelation 5:1-14","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_006_f543cc3568ee91b8e1434555"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}